# Nimpass backend — DEVELOPMENT / TESTNET
#
# This template is the local Testnet workflow. Production values live in
# `.env.production.example`, which is Mainnet and a separate file on purpose.
# The two are not interchangeable: config validation binds APP_ENV to
# NIMIQ_NETWORK, so `production` requires MAINNET and `development`/`test`
# require TESTNET, and the server refuses any other pairing.

APP_ENV=development
HTTP_ADDR=:8080
DATABASE_URL=postgres://nimpass:replace-me@localhost:5432/nimpass?sslmode=disable
NIMIQ_NETWORK=TESTNET
# Must be an address-indexing HISTORY node. Beyond getTransactionByHash, the
# desktop QR checkout needs getTransactionsByAddress: that payment is made
# inside Nimiq Pay with no client able to report a hash, so the backend finds it
# by querying the provider's payout address (docs/DECISIONS.md ADR-010).
# The local node started by ./scripts/testnet-node.sh is the default.
# https://rpc.testnet.nimiqwatch.com is the public Testnet history gateway and
# works as a drop-in (its Mainnet sibling is https://rpc.nimiqwatch.com — note
# that these are two different hosts serving two different chains, and pointing
# a Testnet deployment at the Mainnet one fails startup rather than settling
# anything). Both are public and rate-limited: 20 tokens per fixed 10-second
# window per IP, 429 beyond that. A 429 is treated as "we did not look", never
# as "there is no payment".
NIMIQ_RPC_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8648
PUBLIC_ORIGIN=http://localhost:5173
SESSION_COOKIE_MODE=local-insecure
# Optional comma-separated CIDRs for reverse proxies that are allowed to
# supply X-Forwarded-For. Leave empty when the server is directly exposed.
TRUSTED_PROXY_CIDRS=
# Integration tests use a disposable PostgreSQL database, never production.
TEST_DATABASE_URL=

# Which envelope Nimiq Pay signs: raw | hub
#
# This is the DEFAULT scheme, applied to any proof that does not name one —
# which in practice means every signature from the Nimiq Pay Mini App provider.
# A proof produced by the Nimiq Hub names "hub" itself, because the Hub
# documents its envelope; see docs/DECISIONS.md ADR-003. So this value governs
# the Mini App path only, and changing it cannot break desktop login.
#
# The Mini Apps API reference documents sign()'s parameters and its
# {publicKey, signature} result but not what the host signs, and
# @nimiq/mini-app-sdk forwards the message untouched. Settle it once from a
# device capture and set it here:
#
#   go run ./cmd/verify-sign-fixture -scheme auto \
#     -message '<exact challenge message>' -wallet 'NQ.. ....' \
#     -public-key <hex> -signature <hex>
#
# raw = signature over the message bytes as handed to sign()
# hub = signature over the Nimiq signed-message envelope
NIMIQ_SIGNING_SCHEME=raw

# How much chain certainty a payment must have before the Pass is issued:
#   inclusion | finality        (default: inclusion)
#
# inclusion  The Pass is issued once the payment is canonically included in a
#            micro block and has passed the whole verifier. Albatross produces
#            one roughly every second. Finality is then tracked in the
#            background: the receipt is stored as INCLUDED and promoted to
#            FINALIZED when its macro block is observed.
#
# finality   The Pass waits for the macro block that makes that inclusion
#            irreversible. Macro blocks sit at fixed multiples of the batch
#            length, so this is a uniform nought-to-sixty-second wait on
#            Mainnet for a payment that is already on chain.
#
# This governs the WAIT, never the VALIDATION. Network, recipient, exact Luna,
# NP1 reference or sending wallet, execution result, canonical inclusion, the
# intent's window and global hash uniqueness are all required either way, and a
# mempool transaction settles nothing under either value.
#
# What `inclusion` trades: for under a minute the Pass exists on evidence that
# is canonical but not yet irreversible, and nothing gates redemption on that.
# A settlement the chain later reverses withdraws the Pass and opens a
# compensation case with doNotPayAgain=false, because no NIM ever left the
# wallet. See docs/DECISIONS.md ADR-021.
#
# An unrecognised value fails startup rather than resolving to something.
NIMIQ_CONFIRMATION_POLICY=inclusion

# Ship the forward-only migration files alongside the server.
MIGRATIONS_DIR=migrations
# Production DATABASE_URL must explicitly use sslmode=require, verify-ca, or verify-full.
# Each database is bound to its first server network/environment. Use separate databases.

# Directory for re-encoded pass covers. Filenames are generated UUIDs, never
# the original upload name (docs/09-SECURITY.md §83, docs/08-ARCHITECTURE.md §116).
MEDIA_DIR=var/media
